--synopsis  
Slogans spread because they sound good, and appear to convey meaning.
They also act as a badge that displays a moral stance. 
--synopsis  
  
more_label: Lyrics    
    
--more  
[Static clicks]  
[Intro: Paper rustling]  
(Here is the News!)  
  
[Verse 1 : rapid fire / slogan barrage]  
No one is illegal on stolen land  
All cops are bad, no context, hand to hand  
Metal lives matter, louder than before  
Silence is violence, noise is law  
(do it do it do it)  
  
Trust the science, question power  
Eat the rich in a golden hour  
Peak oil’s dead, peak oil’s back  
Post-truth chorus, verbal attack  
(do it do it do it)  
  
Free speech zone, hate speech crime  
History ends every other time  
Decarbonise, don’t touch my car  
Global village, tribal scar  
(do it do it do it)  
  
[Verse 2 : faster, denser]  
Globalise the intifada  
Hashtag wisdom, instant nada  
Net neutral, carbon sink  
Blink once, blink twice, don’t think  
(do it do it do it)  
  
Safe space, unsafe words  
Signal flares for fragile herds  
Deconstruct the family home  
Where have all the good ones gone?  
(follow follow, follow follow)   
  
Borderless love: gated hearts  
Everything falls into parts  
Raise the voice, shut the gate  
Clap on cue, smash the state  
(Is your brain an autonomous zone?)  
  
[Interlude: Loud thunderclap]  
[instrumental break: virtuoso synth pitch-bending display of talent]  
  
[Pre-Chorus – tightening coil]  
Say it shorter  
Say it cleaner  
Say it like a moral subpoena  
Say it now  
Say it fast  
Say it like it’s built to last  
  
[Chorus – smooth, human, expansive choral backing singers]  
Ideas take each other’s hands  
Round the fire, round the lands  
Not alone, they travel well  
Threaded stories we can’t unspell  
  
Memes don’t walk one by one  
They braid together when they run  
Spinning wide in borrowed skin  
A midsummer dance, where thoughts begin  
  
[drop: glassy synth lead glissando]  
  
[Verse 3 :  weak firmness, still relentless]  
Speak Truth to Power, listen to me:  
New laws enforce cohesion of society  
Emergency powers, just for now  
Watch your step, take the vow  
(you must obey) (obey, obey) (obey)  
  
Context matters, except today  
Read the room, then look away  
Every map’s a battlefield  
Every word a concealed yield  
(logocentric reconstruction) (is the new meta)  
  
Ancient scratchings, prison wall  
Same old jokes, same old call  
Taxes unfair, gods are late  
Kilns still firing bureau-crate  
(Mesopotamia)  
  
[Bridge : half spoken, half sung]  
Not a hive, not a void  
Not a script to be deployed  
Meaning lingers, meaning slips  
Rides in bundles, rides in ships  
(Decolonize West Papua)  
  
Not the word that ends the fight  
Not the silence dressed as right  
Something travels, something sticks  
Not truth, but what replicates  
(think for yourselves, sheeple)  
  
[Chorus : epic side-chained synthwave extasy ]  
Ideas take each other’s hands  
Cross the years, cross the sands  
Carried forward, bent but true  
Old complaints made new  
  
Not commandments carved in stone  
More like seeds the wind has blown  
Some take root, some fall apart  
Still they move, plasmid to heart  
  
[Outro]  
Simulacra are not real  
Even if they make you feel.  
The search for authenticity  
Occurs between you and me.  
(there is only now)  
  
--more    
